19
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.370
What is that? And does it mean that I can ever

20
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.620
go back and become self-centered and self-sovereign again?

21
00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:17.830
Well, let's talk about that. All right?

22
00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.640
In Hebrews chapter 12, we're going to look at verse number 15.

23
00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:25.440
All right? So right after the writer of the Hebrews says

24
00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:26.400
to

25
00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.820
make every effort to live in peace with everyone and to be holy, for without

26
00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:32.200
holiness, no one will see the Lord.

27
00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.650
The next thing he says is,

28
00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:38.380
"See to it that no one falls short of the grace of God."

29
00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.300
Okay, so the full possibilities of grace.

30
00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:45.700
So if Bill Gates offered to buy you a car and said money was no object,

31
00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.180
you wouldn't settle for a used Volkswagen.

32
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.780
You want everything. "See to it that no one falls

33
00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.400
short of the grace of God and that no bitter root

34
00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.650
grows up to cause trouble and defile many."

35
00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.170
Let's unpack that a little bit because I believe that what he's doing there is

36
00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:09.160
using an analogy, a metaphor for the

37
00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:12.960
sin nature. And he says, "See to it that no bitter root

38
00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.900
springs up," and bears bitter fruit, basically,

39
00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:21.300
and causes the defiling of many. Let me give you an analogy, all right?

40
00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:25.460
Let's use this analogy, and it isn't a perfect one, but I think it's an

41
00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.740
appropriate one. Let me see if I can explain.

42
00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.540
So in your life, let's imagine that the tree of

43
00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.440
sin is in your life, all right? And that out of this

44
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.400
nature of sin, this root system, all sorts of evil is

45
00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.800
produced. So you have the

46
00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:47.940
tree of sin producing nature of sin, producing actions of sin in your

47
00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.820
life. Right? And so in salvation, praise God,

48
00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:55.160
Jesus comes along and cuts off this

49
00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:58.850
tree. Thank the Lord. I'm glad to hear that it can happen, right?

50
00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.690
That God can cut off and deal with all of those actions and that

51
00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.720
living in sin in our life. And yet, you know

52
00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.000
what happens if you've ever cut a tree down

53
00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:12.820
and the tree still was alive and healthy at the time.

54
00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:15.700
You know what happens after that. Right?

55
00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:20.260
I just had to do it with one of my trees a while back because I cut one down, and

56
00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.880
all these little sprigs started coming up from the stump.

57
00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:24.780
Over here, they're all growing up.

58
00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.410
And what's going to happen is,

59
00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.100
if I don't take care of that, there's going to be a new tree,

60
00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:33.680
and I'm going to step on more of those little annoying

61
00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:38.049
spiky balls in my backyard. I'm going to have lots

62
00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:38.530
more

63
00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.140
fruit coming that I don't want from the

64
00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.780
life that is still in

65
00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:46.660
this right here.

66
00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:50.060
There's going to be more results from that.

67
00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:50.860
Now,

68
00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:55.290
the next thing that people say then is, well, if the tree is cut down,

69
00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:59.980
and if by grace, God can not just deal with the acts

70
00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.980
of sin, but also the power of it, the presence of it

71
00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:07.320
in my life, not just actions, but nature as well.

72
00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:11.360
If God can take out not just the tree, but also the

73
00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:11.820
stump,

74
00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:13.500
then what?

75
00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:18.921
Well, let me push the analogy just a little bit further, okay?

76
00:04:19.399 --> 00:04:20.260
And you

77
00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:25.600
can only push analogies so far because they get into unbiblical

78
00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:28.620
things, but I think this may be helpful for you to understand.

79
00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:34.300
This fruit, if you've ever known what a tree does, you've ever had an apple tree in

80
00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:36.599
your backyard, it drops fruit.

81
00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.840
Right? It drops apples all over the place.

82
00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:46.040
And when you drop that fruit, it's nasty, and it

83
00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.460
attracts bugs, and it squishes and gets

84
00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:51.520
under your feet and gets your shoes nasty,

85
00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.020
and smells bad, and it rots.

86
00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:59.460
And I would just tell you that after this is cut down,

87
00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:04.600
and after the nature of sin has been removed from your heart,

88
00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.520
what next? Well,

89
00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.410
you're walking along in your life, and you step on something,

90
00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.100
and it squishes.

91
00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.780
You know what I'm talking about? You know the tree is gone.

92
00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.040
You know by God's grace, you believe, and you trust that God

93
00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.830
has done what He promised and removed the nature, cleansed the

94
00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.780
nature of sin from your heart by straightening you back out

95
00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.640
so that you love God with all your heart, soul, mind, and strength, not just

96
00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.960
partially, not with a divided heart, but with a whole one.

97
00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.000
And you step on something that squishes.

98
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:37.940
What are you supposed to do with that?

99
00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:38.960
Well,

100
00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:43.370
here's the thing. What I want to ask, what I want to encourage you to ask is, and

101
00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.260
I'm going to write this on here real quick because if we were sitting across the

102
00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.670
coffee shop table, I would do this.

103
00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:49.820
Is it a root,

104
00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:52.620
or is it a fruit?

105
00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:56.940
What I just found in my life,

106
00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:01.560
that attitude, that action, that thought pattern, that

107
00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.120
way I responded, that way of being in the world right now,

108
00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:09.060
that I'm not happy with that. I feel like it was wrong. It was sinful.

109
00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:10.930
Was it a root

110
00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:14.530
or was it a fruit?

111
00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:20.480
Was it this right here? I found something that squished still in my life or was it

112
00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:23.890
the other? Let me give you another analogy for this or another idea

113
00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:24.950
here.

114
00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.270
We have two different things that we're dealing with here.

115
00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.790
One is self-sovereignty, and the essence of the sin

116
00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:35.870
nature is self-will, self-sovereignty.

117
00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:40.110
I want to be in charge. That's the essence of the sin nature.

118
00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:41.240
Now,

119
00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:46.330
self-centeredness can be these patterns

120
00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:47.610
up here.

121
00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:52.230
They can be just automatic ways. I automatically assume that the world

122
00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:55.760
revolves around me in my relationships or in my marriage or in my

123
00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:59.290
interactions with my boss or my coworkers.

124
00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:03.230
I just assume that the world revolves around me because that's the way

125
00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:05.390
I've always thought.

126
00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.610
And even after Jesus deals with this,

127
00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.230
there's still some

128
00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:16.830
self-centered patterns and thoughts and

129
00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:20.840
ways of behaving in my life that I've never even noticed before.

130
00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:24.630
I'm not conscious of them. They're just present because God hasn't

131
00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:27.290
pointed them out to me yet. And I'm walking along

132
00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.570
and something squishes and smells bad,

133
00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:32.210
and it's nasty.

134
00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:36.530
What do I do? Here's what I do. I say, "Is that a root?"

135
00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.910
Am I self-sovereign in this area and am I just wanting my way

136
00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:44.810
regardless of what God says? Or is it just a pattern of

137
00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:46.640
self-centeredness that I've never noticed before,

138
00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:51.500
but I want to scoop up right now and I'm going to get rid of it because I don't

139
00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.190
want any bitter roots growing up in my life.

140
00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:58.630
I don't want the seeds of sin in that bad habit that I've

141
00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:02.450
never noticed before. I don't want those seeds to germinate and

142
00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:06.390
create a new bitter root that springs up and bears bitter

143
00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:07.790
fruit in my life.

144
00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:09.510
So here's what you do.

145
00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:14.190
Is it a root or is it a fruit? If the Lord says to you, "Yes, you're

146
00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:17.360
still self-sovereign. You want your way regardless."

147
00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:22.200
If that's true, then let's be filled with the Holy Spirit and let's take care of

148
00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:23.830
that. Let's get rid of the sin nature.

149
00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:25.290
If it's not true,

150
00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:30.030
then let's scoop up the old rotten fruit of self-centeredness and let's get rid of

151
00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.850
it. Let's not say, "Well, that can't be rotten fruit.

152
00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:37.030
I know I'm holy. I know I'm made holy. I'm filled with the Holy Spirit.

153
00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:39.910
Can't be for me. I don't have any room." Oh, no.

154
00:08:41.451 --> 00:08:44.710
Let's be honest and let's say, "That was wrong."

155
00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:49.590
I've got a pattern there of self-centered behavior and thinking, and I

156
00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:53.090
need to scoop that up and get rid of it, or it'll germinate, and I'll have a

157
00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.750
brand-new root of bitterness springing up.

158
00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:57.270
You need to be honest with yourself,

159
00:08:58.090 --> 00:09:01.570
and you need to deal with it, but don't throw away your confidence in what God has

160
00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:04.670
done for you. Don't cast it out just because you found something.

161
00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:08.730
Let's be honest. Let's deal with it, and then let's move on

162
00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:11.810
forward. That's what I wanted to share with you today. God bless.

163
00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:12.910
Talk to you next time.
